issue_context.body:
If the customization string is 127 bytes it passes the check. Then `kmac_init()` calls `bytepad()`, with in1_len=6, in2_len=130, and w=136. `bytepad()` tries to pad the buffer with 134 zero bytes.
``` C
/* zero pad the end of the buffer */
memset(p, 0, sz - len);
```
The buffer can only hold 168 bytes and there are already 138 bytes in the buffer This is what the check in `kmac_set_ctx_params()` was trying to protect against.
